[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Sharing [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mWhat's the unit of sharing for tasks?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mProjects with members (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mTasks belong to a project; users are members of projects. Membership drives both visibility and the later 'watch [39m
     [38;5;246mthis' subscription model.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Per-task sharing
     [38;5;246mEach task has an owner and an explicit list of people it is shared with. Granular, but no natural grouping and [39m
     [38;5;246mtedious at volume.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m One global workspace
     [38;5;246mEveryone sees all tasks; assignment is the only relationship. Simplest schema, no privacy, little to subscribe to.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Projects plus per-task guests
     [38;5;246mProjects are the main unit, but individual tasks can also be shared with non-members. More flexible, more [39m
     [38;5;246mpermission logic to get right.[39m
  [38;5;246m5. Type something.[39m
